{
  "notes": [
    "Map weather: prototype content, not from the books. A map saves one weather id; maps saved before weather existed are Clear.",
    "Outdoor locations offer their biome's weathers (byBiome). Indoor locations (every 'space' and 'interior' location plus indoorLocations) ignore the biome and offer their own atmospheres (byLocation).",
    "byBiome / byLocation: the weathers on offer, with Generate Map's odds (relative weights). The editor lists only those weathers. Barren worlds are drawn airless (biomes.json card skies), so they get no rain, snow or fog.",
    "fx: what src/effects/WeatherFx.jsx draws over the map (layer kinds in src/effects/weatherKinds.js). tint: a colour wash over the whole view. layers run in order. density: particles per 10,000 screen pixels. speed: pixels per second. angle: degrees from straight down (positive leans right). Colours written 'r, g, b' get their alpha from the effect.",
    "Layer kinds: rain (streaks; length, width), sand (fast streaks; length, width), snow (drifting flakes; size, sway), ash (slow flakes; embers = share that glow and rise), fog (drifting banks), sparks (bursts from emitters points every [min, max] s, falling under gravity), bolt (jagged branching lightning every [min, max] s), glints (twinkling points; twinkle rate, size, sideways speed), aurora (waving ribbons across the top; colours, height, alpha, speed), ripple (rings spreading on the ground every [min, max] s; life, radius, alpha), vortex (dust devils; count, grains, grainSize, radius, height, spin, speed), meteors (count streaks; speed [min, max], angle, length, every [min, max] s between them), scanlines (faint lines creeping down; spacing, speed, alpha, glitch bands every [min, max] s). An angle of 180 makes snow / ash rise instead of fall; a negative fog speed drifts left.",
    "flash: a full-screen flicker of colour (r, g, b) every [min, max] seconds; black flashes read as a power flicker. pulse: a colour (r, g, b) that breathes between alpha [min, max] every period seconds.",
    "Generate Card paints a still frame of the map's weather onto the picture. On the ground it picks the sky from the biome's card skies (biomes.json), narrowed to the weather's cardSkies, or to stormySkies for weather with rain, snow, sand or fog layers or a strong tint; when none of those suit the biome it uses the biome's own skies."
  ],
  "default": "clear",
  "stormySkies": ["overcast", "murky", "dusk", "night", "volcanic", "airless"],
  "indoorLocations": ["cave"],
